@!internal

--- The system calls under the native core's file layer, as its host answers
--- them. A call of one is the core's own library call, and requiring this
--- module loads nothing: it exists only on the core, for `nupp.runtime.files`.
--- Each answers what the system call did: a descriptor, count or position,
--- or the negated error number.
local record filecalls
    --- Opens the file at `path` with the access `flags` asks for: 1 read,
    --- 2 write, 4 create, 8 truncate and 16 append, added together. A file
    --- it creates gets mode 0666, less the umask.
    open: function(path: string, flags: integer): integer

    --- At most `count` bytes read from `descriptor`, "" at its end.
    read: function(descriptor: integer, count: integer): string | integer

    --- Writes `text` from its byte `first` on to `descriptor`: the count
    --- written, which may be fewer.
    write: function(descriptor: integer, text: string, first: integer): integer

    --- Moves `descriptor` to `offset` from its start (0), its position (1)
    --- or its end (2): the new position.
    seek: function(descriptor: integer, offset: integer, whence: integer): integer

    --- Closes `descriptor`, which is gone even when this fails.
    close: function(descriptor: integer): integer

    --- The system's text for error number `code`, C's strerror.
    reason: function(code: integer): string
end

local calls: filecalls
return calls
